<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπηνέμ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lifted</i> or <i>wafted by the wind,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπᾱνέμιοι φορέονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					5.115
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τανύοιτο,</span> of the Sun,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				839
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>swift as the wind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sert.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>full of wind,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ᾠὰ</span>
			<i>wind</i>-eggs, which produce no chickens, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				186
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				19
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμιαῖον ᾠόν</span> was
			considered better 
				Att.
			, Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.73
			</span></i> P.); of eggs laid by hens without impregnation, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				559b24
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυήματα ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>GA</u>
					749b1
				</span></i>
			; in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				695
			</span></i> (anap.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ᾠόν</span> is the
			egg produced by Night <i>alone,</i> without impregnation; and
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				6
			</span></i> calls Hephaestus the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ.
			παῖς</span> of Hera; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχεῖαι καὶ ὠδῖνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.38e
				</span></i>
			 (s. v.l.): hence </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., <i>empty, idle,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνειροι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				735e
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῦτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Gall.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
